{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791635975,"nonce":"oze68igimaBmTBKgEYPInHILDnw=","message":"Measured again 2026-10-10 at ashui 2b0c2a6 (blinc_abi a605700; Ash 3d5ab48, application preset, hybrid; footprint -p 40 s after launch, idle). Interactions 92 MB, Canvas2D 213 MB, from 169 and about 300-350 on 10-05. The gap is about 121 MB.\n\n| category | Interactions | Canvas2D | extra |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| MALLOC_SMALL | 53 MB | 96 MB | +43 |\n| owned unmapped (graphics) | 3.6 MB | 37 MB | +33 |\n| VM_ALLOCATE (GC heap) | 9 MB | 36 MB | +27 |\n| IOSurface | 13 MB | 25 MB | +12 |\n| MALLOC_LARGE | 1 MB | 5 MB | +4 |\n\n**GPU, +33 MB**\nCanvas2D makes two 2200x1440 layer targets, a content layer and the backdrop-rows intermediate, for its toolbar's backdrop blur: about 12.7 MB each. Interactions makes none. Its canvas data texture is 2044x2 Rgba32float, which is negligible. Every layer target is window-sized whatever the effect covers.\nProposed fix: size a layer to the effect's bounds plus the blur's reach. Its passes then draw with an origin offset, and the composite samples with that offset. A toolbar-sized backdrop would take well under 1 MB.\n\n**MALLOC_SMALL, +43 MB** (heap -sortBySize under MallocStackLogging=lite, Canvas2D less Interactions)\n- +20.3 MB \"non-object from xgpu.hdll\": 20,338 blocks of about 1 KB. Sampled backtraces go through __hl_gpu_device_create_shader: wgpu shader modules, whose naga IR wgpu-core keeps while their pipelines live. Canvas2D builds more pipelines (canvas paths, meshes and layers), and each HXSL shader carries the whole Sdf library. hlwgpu 0d9a25c tracks the source expansion; fewer, shared modules would cut this.\n- +4.2 and +1.0 MB ColorSync TRC tables: colour management for the larger window's surface.\n- About +8 MB of Ash AIR, LLVM and JIT allocations: Canvas2D runs more code. That is Ash's f60b855 family.\n\n**VM_ALLOCATE, +27 MB**\nThe GC heap holding the demo's own objects (paths, meshes, display lists): Haxe allocations, not a native leak.\n\n**IOSurface, +12 MB**\nThe window's drawables: Canvas2D's window is larger.\n\nNext: the bounded-layer change above is the main ashui-side saving.","files":null}]}